      "content": "but just war theory is kinda vague, right? like it says \"extraordinary circumstances\" but doesn't really say if protecting human rights or democracy is actually more important than a country's sovereignty. if we know a dictator is about to take over and commit atrocities, isn't it more \"moral\" to strike first rather than just sitting back and letting it happen? give me a straight answer on whether human rights should override national sovereignty in these cases.",
